 "captions": [
  {
   "at": 0.0,
   "until": 2.4,
   "text": "The market may be labeling the wrong bubble."
  },
  {
   "at": 2.4,
   "until": 5.77,
   "text": "AI memory stocks have gone vertical and the earnings numbers"
  },
  {
   "at": 5.77,
   "until": 9.53,
   "text": "look almost fake. That is normally where sensible people step"
  },
  {
   "at": 9.53,
   "until": 12.87,
   "text": "back and say: bubble. But underneath the chart"
  },
  {
   "at": 12.87,
   "until": 15.47,
   "text": "is a product customers cannot get enough of,"
  },
  {
   "at": 15.47,
   "until": 19.07,
   "text": "factories that cannot expand quickly enough, and buyers signing"
  },
  {
   "at": 19.07,
   "until": 23.03,
   "text": "multi-year take-or-pay contracts just to guarantee supply."
  },
  {
   "at": 23.03,
   "until": 25.67,
   "text": "Meanwhile, the trade marketed as boring and"
  },
  {
   "at": 25.67,
   "until": 28.6,
   "text": "diversified\u2014the S&P 500 index"
  },
  {
   "at": 28.6,
   "until": 31.97,
   "text": "fund\u2014has nearly forty percent of its weight concentrated in"
  },
  {
   "at": 31.97,
   "until": 35.7,
   "text": "ten companies, while automatic contributions keep buying them"
  },
  {
   "at": 35.7,
   "until": 39.13,
   "text": "because they are already the biggest. So here is the argument:"
  },
  {
   "at": 39.13,
   "until": 42.1,
   "text": "the memory trade can absolutely correct."
  },
  {
   "at": 42.1,
   "until": 45.77,
   "text": "It can become overpriced. It can still be brutally cyclical."
  },
  {
   "at": 45.77,
   "until": 49.87,
   "text": "But what we are seeing today looks more like a physical bottleneck being repriced"
  },
  {
   "at": 49.87,
   "until": 53.03,
   "text": "than a demand-free fantasy. Bubble logic may be"
  },
  {
   "at": 53.03,
   "until": 56.17,
   "text": "hiding inside the thing investors stopped examining because"
  },
  {
   "at": 56.17,
   "until": 58.03,
   "text": "they were told it was safe."
  },
  {
   "at": 58.03,
   "until": 61.57,
   "text": "A bubble is not \u201ca price went up a lot.\u201d"
  },
  {
   "at": 61.57,
   "until": 64.87,
   "text": "That is a symptom, not a diagnosis."
  },
  {
   "at": 64.87,
   "until": 68.73,
   "text": "A real bubble forms when the price increasingly depends on the belief that"
  },
  {
   "at": 68.73,
   "until": 71.8,
   "text": "somebody else will pay more, while the cash flow,"
  },
  {
   "at": 71.8,
   "until": 74.8,
   "text": "productive use, or scarcity underneath it cannot"
  },
  {
   "at": 74.8,
   "until": 78.93,
   "text": "keep up. Think of two elevators rising at the same speed."
  },
  {
   "at": 78.93,
   "until": 82.77,
   "text": "One is being pulled by a steel cable. The other is rising because"
  },
  {
   "at": 82.77,
   "until": 86.17,
   "text": "everyone inside jumped at once. The chart looks identical"
  },
  {
   "at": 86.17,
   "until": 89.8,
   "text": "for half a second. The mechanism is completely different."
  },
  {
   "at": 89.8,
   "until": 92.83,
   "text": "So we need to look under both elevators. For memory,"
  },
  {
   "at": 92.83,
   "until": 97.3,
   "text": "the cables are demand, capacity, contracts, and cash flow."
  },
  {
   "at": 97.3,
   "until": 100.97,
   "text": "For the S&P 500 complex, the question is whether diversification"
  },
  {
   "at": 100.97,
   "until": 104.2,
   "text": "has quietly become concentration\u2014and whether automatic"
  },
  {
   "at": 104.2,
   "until": 108.17,
   "text": "demand is helping investors ignore the price of that concentration."
  },
  {
   "at": 108.17,
   "until": 111.3,
   "text": "Start with the product. High-bandwidth memory,"
  },
  {
   "at": 111.3,
   "until": 113.97,
   "text": "or HBM, is not ordinary storage."
  },
  {
   "at": 113.97,
   "until": 117.7,
   "text": "It is stacked working memory placed beside an AI accelerator so"
  },
  {
   "at": 117.7,
   "until": 121.1,
   "text": "enormous amounts of data can reach the processor quickly."
  },
  {
   "at": 121.1,
   "until": 123.9,
   "text": "Plain English: the GPU may be the engine,"
  },
  {
   "at": 123.9,
   "until": 126.93,
   "text": "but HBM is the pressure-rated fuel system."
  },
  {
   "at": 126.93,
   "until": 130.77,
   "text": "Build a larger engine without widening the fuel line and the expensive engine"
  },
  {
   "at": 130.77,
   "until": 134.07,
   "text": "sits there starving. That is why every serious AI"
  },
  {
   "at": 134.07,
   "until": 137.57,
   "text": "architecture\u2014whether it uses GPUs, custom accelerators,"
  },
  {
   "at": 137.57,
   "until": 141.03,
   "text": "or specialized processors\u2014has to solve memory bandwidth and"
  },
  {
   "at": 141.03,
   "until": 144.6,
   "text": "capacity. And this is where the shortage becomes physical."
  },
  {
   "at": 144.6,
   "until": 148.4,
   "text": "HBM competes for advanced wafers, clean-room space,"
  },
  {
   "at": 148.4,
   "until": 151.37,
   "text": "packaging capacity, equipment, engineers,"
  },
  {
   "at": 151.37,
   "until": 154.73,
   "text": "and time. New generations also use"
  },
  {
   "at": 154.73,
   "until": 157.9,
   "text": "larger dies and more complicated stacks."
  },
  {
   "at": 157.9,
   "until": 160.97,
   "text": "Imagine a bakery with a fixed number of ovens."
  },
  {
   "at": 160.97,
   "until": 163.77,
   "text": "Yesterday it made simple loaves. Today its most"
  },
  {
   "at": 163.77,
   "until": 166.9,
   "text": "valuable customer wants twelve-layer wedding cakes."
  },
  {
   "at": 166.9,
   "until": 170.9,
   "text": "Each cake earns more, but it also occupies more oven space,"
  },
  {
   "at": 170.9,
   "until": 174.6,
   "text": "takes longer, and has more opportunities to fail."
  },
  {
   "at": 174.6,
   "until": 178.1,
   "text": "Producing more cakes can mean producing fewer loaves."
  },
  {
   "at": 178.1,
   "until": 181.77,
   "text": "As manufacturers devote more capacity to HBM,"
  },
  {
   "at": 181.77,
   "until": 185.13,
   "text": "they also pressure conventional DRAM supply."
  },
  {
   "at": 185.13,
   "until": 189.3,
   "text": "The AI boom pulls the same production system toward more complex products."
  },
  {
   "at": 189.3,
   "until": 192.6,
   "text": "Micron says HBM\u2019s growing trade ratio is pressuring"
  },
  {
   "at": 192.6,
   "until": 196.2,
   "text": "non-HBM supply and new fabs take years."
  },
  {
   "at": 196.2,
   "until": 199.73,
   "text": "Samsung says concentrating capacity on HBM and server"
  },
  {
   "at": 199.73,
   "until": 203.57,
   "text": "products limits cutting-edge supply for PCs and phones."
  },
  {
   "at": 203.57,
   "until": 206.37,
   "text": "This is not proof that any stock price is fair."
  },
  {
   "at": 206.37,
   "until": 210.17,
   "text": "It is proof that the underlying shortage is not imaginary."
  },
  {
   "at": 210.17,
   "until": 213.23,
   "text": "Now look at buyer behavior. In a classic commodity"
  },
  {
   "at": 213.23,
   "until": 217.13,
   "text": "memory cycle, suppliers add capacity, prices spike,"
  },
  {
   "at": 217.13,
   "until": 221.8,
   "text": "everybody gets excited, too much supply arrives, and margins collapse."
  },
  {
   "at": 221.8,
   "until": 225.47,
   "text": "That history is the strongest argument against this entire video."
  },
  {
   "at": 225.47,
   "until": 228.27,
   "text": "But customers are behaving differently this time."
  },
  {
   "at": 228.27,
   "until": 231.87,
   "text": "Micron says it has completed sixteen strategic customer"
  },
  {
   "at": 231.87,
   "until": 236.4,
   "text": "agreements across data centers, consumer devices, and automotive markets."
  },
  {
   "at": 236.4,
   "until": 239.67,
   "text": "Most run for five years. They cover roughly twenty percent of"
  },
  {
   "at": 239.67,
   "until": 242.8,
   "text": "its DRAM volume and one-third of its NAND volume over"
  },
  {
   "at": 242.8,
   "until": 246.27,
   "text": "the contract period. They are take-or-pay agreements: buyers commit"
  },
  {
   "at": 246.27,
   "until": 249.97,
   "text": "to specific volumes rather than casually promising they might show up"
  },
  {
   "at": 249.97,
   "until": 253.4,
   "text": "later. Translation: customers are reserving"
  },
  {
   "at": 253.4,
   "until": 255.73,
   "text": "oven time through 2030."
  },
  {
   "at": 255.73,
   "until": 259.13,
   "text": "SK hynix reported record first-quarter performance driven by"
  },
  {
   "at": 259.13,
   "until": 263.53,
   "text": "AI memory, high-capacity server DRAM, and enterprise SSDs,"
  },
  {
   "at": 263.53,
   "until": 267.07,
   "text": "while saying demand exceeded supply capacity."
  },
  {
   "at": 267.07,
   "until": 270.27,
   "text": "Samsung began commercial HBM4 shipments and expects"
  },
  {
   "at": 270.27,
   "until": 273.83,
   "text": "its HBM sales to more than triple in 2026."
  },
  {
   "at": 273.83,
   "until": 277.3,
   "text": "Company guidance is not gospel. But contracts, shipments,"
  },
  {
   "at": 277.3,
   "until": 280.3,
   "text": "and reported revenue are stronger evidence than clicks,"
  },
  {
   "at": 280.3,
   "until": 283.33,
   "text": "token prices, or a pitch deck promising a market that does"
  },
  {
   "at": 283.33,
   "until": 286.63,
   "text": "not exist. That is why I would call this a bottleneck boom"
  },
  {
   "at": 286.63,
   "until": 288.33,
   "text": "before I call it a bubble."
  },
  {
   "at": 288.33,
   "until": 291.0,
   "text": "This is also bigger than three memory companies."
  },
  {
   "at": 291.0,
   "until": 294.5,
   "text": "The world economy is reorganizing around strategic chokepoints:"
  },
  {
   "at": 294.5,
   "until": 298.0,
   "text": "advanced chips, memory, packaging, power equipment, robotics,"
  },
  {
   "at": 298.0,
   "until": 300.0,
   "text": "and defense technology. Capital markets are beginning to raise"
  }
 ],
